GoldLink's change to melonDS (UC11): what the lighting needs from a frame.

- GPU3D_Soft: GetWideDepthLine gives the wide 3D line's depth buffer (as GetWideLine its colour);
  GetShownDepthLine the depth of the picture on screen. The next frame's 3D is rendered at line
  215, before the frame ends, so the depth buffer is a frame ahead of the screen by then:
  RenderFrame keeps a copy of the shown one before it renders.
- GPU3D: the projection matrix most of a frame's polygons were drawn with (a frame can end on a
  pass with its own, such as a 2D overlay), kept with the frame through the swap and the render
  (RenderProjMatrix, then ShownProjMatrix), and whether the frame on screen used W-buffering.
- The smooth camera: when the game shows a new 3D scene after repeating the last one (its 30 a
  second), the halfway picture is made from the game's own drawing commands. GPU3D logs each
  scene's command words and keeps a savestate of the engine as each scene starts
  (RecordScenes); GPU3D_Soft replays the new scene's words on a copy of the engine from that
  state (Replay: no interrupts, DMA or stalls), each matrix parameter part way from the same word
  of the last scene (where the camera has moved a whole number of pixels: its step between the
  two pictures, halved and rounded down, so things keep their places in the pixel grid) (the scenes lined up word by word; a matrix pairs only with a near one), lets
  the copy's swap sort the polygons,
  and renders them into its own buffers (MidColor, MidDepth). GPU2D_Soft composes that picture
  line by line as it composes the frame (MidPicture): the same backgrounds, sprites, effects and
  side strips over the halfway 3D picture. While it's on, the 3D view has a margin past the
  picture (the shim widens GPU3D::WideSide by 8; GPU3D::TallSide adds 8 rows above and below as
  WideSide adds columns: clip-space y scaled, the buffers RenderHeight rows, the line readers
  offset), so what's just outside the picture is drawn too. Off unless the frontend asks.
- GPU2D_Soft: Layer3D records, per main-engine line, where the 3D layer shows in the composed
  picture (on top, under a 2D layer, or not at all), for the screen and the wide picture's
  side strips; a text box or menu drawn over the 3D scene is left out of the lighting.

Applied by build.rs to a copy of the submodule (which stays at upstream).

